1.Generators in python  

You have a 10–50 GB application log file on a server.  
You need to scan it for errors and send alerts — without crashing the system or using too much memory.  

```
def read_logs(file_path):
    return open(file_path).readlines()  # loads entire file into memory
```

Problems  
Tries to load GBs of data into RAM  
Slow startup  
Can cause OOM (Out Of Memory) errors  

```
def stream_logs(file_path):
    with open(file_path) as file:
        for line in file:
            yield line
```

Reads one log line at a time  
✔ Memory usage stays constant  
✔ Perfect for real-time or near-real-time processing  

```
def find_errors(log_stream):
    for log in log_stream:
        if "ERROR" in log:
            yield log
```

```
for error_log in find_errors(stream_logs("app.log")):
    print("ALERT:", error_log)
```

stream_logs() reads one line from disk  
find_errors() checks it  
If it’s an error, it’s immediately processed  
Memory usage stays low, no matter how large the file is  



